  the second full pass with a finding left open, needing passes >= 2 and deferred >= 1; else REVIEW_LOOP_EXCEPTION_INVALID). Every receipt records gstack_version and
  review_depth: the depth HEAD needs, recomputed from the committed range (--head must be HEAD; a dirty checkout or an
  unreadable input records full).
  --review-exclude <digest|none> (the digest= on gstack-review-dispatch verify's REVIEW_EXCLUDE_RECORD: line, which the reviewers' briefs
  name; none without that line): must equal the digest HEAD has under the base policy's review_exclude_paths, else
  RECEIPT_INVALID field=review_exclude and nothing is written; recorded as review_exclude (HEAD's). Write, carry and the queue also bind
  a digest from an earlier base policy when it gives the PR's files the same selection as HEAD's: the same applied patterns,
  excluded files and kept files with their reasons (GST-1446; write rebuilds it from the policies the base held, prints
  REVIEW_EXCLUDE_POLICY_MOVED:, and refuses when none does; an omitted --review-exclude is never rebuilt).
  The check binds the digest to the base policy, not to a review: write does not read the review ledger, so the expected=
  digest a refusal prints passes too. After a refusal, rerun the review and pass the digest its verify prints.
  --docs-post <audit-id>-post.json (Step 14.5's post snapshot, the file finish takes): the reviewed --review-exclude digest also binds
  when the only change to the selection since the review is files under review_exclude_paths that the snapshot names as uncommitted,
  with the content HEAD holds, each excluded or kept only because code names it (GST-1429); prints REVIEW_EXCLUDE_DOCS_AUDIT: and
  records HEAD's selection. Any other change, or an unreadable snapshot, refuses as above. --docs-pre <Prepare snapshot> (the same
  audit's first snapshot) narrows the audit's files to those whose content it changed, so uncommitted docs the review read stay.
  An audit file the review kept for its own content (gate path, gate tags, agent prose, a secret line) refuses with
  RECEIPT_DOCS_AUDIT_READ and writes a packet of the audit's change for one scoped reader, not a review round (GST-3532);
  --docs-audit-read <record.json> (its clean { head, paths, reviewer, verdict, packet_sha256 }) binds it as docs_audit_read.
  When a run audits twice, the last audit's post snapshot carries the earlier audit (gstack-docs-candidate snapshot --run --pre
  --carry): files the earlier audit edited reset too, to their content before it, when HEAD holds what it left; a carried audit of
  another run refuses (GST-1616).
  --no-stop <json|@file> (a JSON array of {class, reason, evidence}: each routine stop the run recorded and went on past, class one of
  scoped-fix-check, test-timeout-fix, pregate-flake-rerun, autoplan-regate); recorded as no_stop.
  --declare-risk <classes> (the same list gstack-review-plan --declare-risk took): joins review_depth's risk and only raises
  its depth; review_depth.declared and .detected record both lists (GST-1129). An unknown class is RECEIPT_INVALID.
  --platform-review <id> (NEXT: platform's PLATFORM_REVIEW: id): records review_depth platform with capy-ai[bot]'s review <id> at HEAD;
  refused (RECEIPT_INVALID) unless the base policy has review.platform on, HEAD needs light review of a docs or tests diff with
  no numeric, results or prereg claims, and that review is on the PR at HEAD. review_depth.mode records lean, panel or platform.
  --review-targeted <json|@file> ({classes, rules, brief_sha, status, findings, raised_by, head}: gstack-review-dispatch verify
  --targeted-out); recorded as review_targeted bound to the receipt's product_patch_id, and refused (RECEIPT_INVALID) when the
  commit the reader read (head) is not an ancestor or a change since it carries a targeted class (gate scan included). write and carry
  refuse a receipt whose head needs a targeted class (money, gate, auth, secret) that no done pass covers, as the queue's
  targeted verdict does (#3859) (RECEIPT_INVALID, RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED).
  --approval-run <autoplan run dir> (repeatable; resolves plan-sha citations) (W2: a class declared in origin/<base>'s
  .gstack/approval-classes.json with hits needs a citation that resolves and binds to its effects: APPROVAL_CITATION_MISSING)
  --out <file> --body <pr-body.md>. Defaults: head=HEAD, base=origin/HEAD's branch, version=the
  version source at HEAD ("none" when HEAD has no version source, no policy stamp file and no CHANGELOG), session_kind=$GSTACK_SESSION_KIND (gstack-session-kind), tree/gate_reuse/gated_tree/predecessor
  from --receipt when given.
--json: JSON only on stdout.
${exitTableHelp()}`;

function flag(args: string[], name: string): string | undefined {
  const i = args.indexOf(name);
  return i >= 0 ? args[i + 1] : undefined;
}
function flags(args: string[], name: string): string[] {
  return args.flatMap((a, i) => (a === name && args[i + 1] !== undefined ? [args[i + 1]!] : []));
}
function jsonArg(raw: string | undefined): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {
  if (raw === undefined) return undefined;
  const text = raw.startsWith('@') ? fs.readFileSync(raw.slice(1), 'utf8') : raw;
  const parsed = JSON.parse(text);
  if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== 'object' || Array.isArray(parsed)) throw new Error('expected a JSON object');
  return parsed;
}
/** --no-stop <json|@file>: the routine stops this run recorded and went on past (K1), a JSON array of {class, reason, evidence}. */
function noStopArg(raw: string | undefined): ShipReceipt['no_stop'] {
  if (raw === undefined) return undefined;
  const parsed = JSON.parse(raw.startsWith('@') ? fs.readFileSync(raw.slice(1), 'utf8') : raw);
  if (!Array.isArray(parsed)) throw new Error('--no-stop expects a JSON array of {class, reason, evidence}');
  const kept = parsed.filter(r => (NO_STOP_CLASSES as readonly string[]).includes(r?.class) || void process.stderr.write(`NO_STOP: dropped ${JSON.stringify(r?.class)} from --no-stop: not a current no-stop class (${NO_STOP_CLASSES.join(', ')}), so the receipt leaves it out (GST-2706)\n`));
  return kept.length ? kept : undefined;
}
function git(args: string[], cwd?: string): string | undefined {
  const r = spawnSync('git', args, { cwd, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 30_000, maxBuffer: 256 * 1024 * 1024 });
  return r.status === 0 ? r.stdout.trim() : undefined;
}
function gh(args: string[]): { ok: boolean; out: string; err: string } {
  const r = ghSpawnSync(args, { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 120_000, maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024 });
  return { ok: r.status === 0, out: r.stdout ?? '', err: (r.stderr ?? '').trim() };
}

/**
 * The receipt's `version`: the version source at HEAD (the pinned path, else
 * VERSION, else package.json#version). A repository with none of those, no
 * policy stamp file and no CHANGELOG at HEAD has no release version to record,
 * and the receipt says so with `"none"` (docs/ship-policy.md#ship-receipt);
 * `read`, `result` and the queue accept it like any other version string.
 * Only an absent source is `"none"`: a VERSION that exists but holds no
 * parsable version, a pin that escapes the repository, or an unreadable base
 * policy keeps the existing no-version refusal.
 */
function receiptVersion(repoRoot: string, head: string, base: string): string | undefined {
  const atHead = versionAtRef(repoRoot, head);
  if ('version' in atHead) return atHead.version;
  if (!/ does not exist at /.test(atHead.error)) return undefined;
  const show = (rel: string) => git(['show', `${head}:${rel}`], repoRoot);
  try { const v = JSON.parse(show('package.json') ?? 'null')?.version; if (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim()) return v.trim(); } catch { /* not a manifest */ }
  const load = loadPolicyFromBase(repoRoot, base);
  if (isUnavailable(load)) return undefined;
  const changelogs = [...new Set([load.policy.changelog, 'CHANGELOG.md'].filter((p): p is string => !!p))];
  if (stampFilesInTree(repoRoot, head, load.policy.stamp_files).length || changelogs.some(p => show(p) !== undefined)) return undefined;
  return 'none';
}

/**
 * What a later carry across rewritten history compares: the head's tree and its
 * product patch-id against the base. Both are evidence, never a gate: a head
 * outside a checkout (or a base that does not resolve) records neither, and
 * such a receipt then carries only along its own history.
 */
function reviewedProduct(repoRoot: string, base: string, head: string, pregateFile: string | undefined): { head_tree?: string; product_patch_id?: string } {
  const tree = git(['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', `${head}^{tree}`], repoRoot);
  if (!tree) return {};
  const baseRef = `origin/${base.replace(/^origin\//, '')}`;
  const id = productPatchAgainstBase(repoRoot, productRules(repoRoot, base, verifiedOutputs(repoRoot, base, pregateFile)), baseRef, head);
  return typeof id === 'string' ? { head_tree: tree, product_patch_id: id || 'none' } : { head_tree: tree };
}

/** The lanes CI carried at the checked-out tree under origin/<base>'s mapping, from this machine's evidence ledger (gstack-evidence carried); undefined when none. */
function ciCarried(base: string): ShipReceipt['ci_carried'] {
  const r = runScriptSync(path.join(path.dirname(Bun.fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), 'gstack-evidence'), ['carried', '--base', base, '--json'], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 60_000 });
  try { const list = JSON.parse(r.stdout); return Array.isArray(list) && list.length ? list : undefined; } catch { return undefined; }
}

/** calls= (G2): --calls <n>, or the run's count from the call log through its budget record; absent when neither is given or the log holds no row. */
function callsArg(rest: string[]): number | undefined {
  const raw = flag(rest, '--calls');
  if (raw !== undefined) { if (!/^\d+$/.test(raw)) throw new Error(`--calls '${raw}' is not a whole number`); return Number(raw); }
  const record = flag(rest, '--budget-record');
  if (record === undefined) return undefined;
  try { return runCalls(record, process.env) ?? undefined; } catch (e: any) { throw new Error(`--budget-record ${record}: ${e.message}`); }
}

async function cmdWrite(rest: string[], json: boolean): Promise<number> {
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']) ?? process.cwd();
  const checkedOut = git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], repoRoot);
  const head = flag(rest, '--head') ?? checkedOut;
  if (!head) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt write: --head is required outside a git repository\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const headSha = git(['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', `${head}^{commit}`], repoRoot);
  if (checkedOut && headSha !== checkedOut) {
    process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `--head ${head.slice(0, 12)} is not the checked-out HEAD ${checkedOut.slice(0, 12)}; the receipt binds the reviewed tree, so check out ${head.slice(0, 12)} and write there; nothing written`) + '\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  const receiptFile = flag(rest, '--receipt');
  const tree = receiptFile ? JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(receiptFile, 'utf8')) : null;
  let sessionKind = flag(rest, '--session-kind') ?? process.env.GSTACK_SESSION_KIND;
  if (!sessionKind) {
    const r = runScriptSync(path.join(path.dirname(Bun.fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), 'gstack-session-kind'), [], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 15_000 });
    sessionKind = r.status === 0 ? r.stdout.trim() || undefined : undefined;
  }
  let pregate: PregateField | undefined;
  const pregateFile = flag(rest, '--pregate');
  if (pregateFile) {
    const read = pregateFieldFor(repoRoot, pregateFile, head, flag(rest, '--base'));
    if (!read.ok) { for (const e of read.errors) process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', e.code, `${e.message}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
    pregate = read.field;
  }
  const pause = flag(rest, '--base-red') ? readPause(flag(rest, '--base-red')!) : undefined;
  if (typeof pause === 'string') { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt write: --base-red: ${pause}; nothing written\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  const base = flag(rest, '--base') ?? resolveBaseBranch(repoRoot);
  const bodyFile = flag(rest, '--body');
  const bodyText = bodyFile && fs.existsSync(bodyFile) ? fs.readFileSync(bodyFile, 'utf8').replace(/```gstack-ship-receipt[\s\S]*?\n```/g, '') : '';
  let docs: ReturnType<typeof parseReceiptDocs> | undefined;
  if (flag(rest, '--docs') !== undefined) {
    try { docs = parseReceiptDocs(jsonArg(flag(rest, '--docs'))); } catch (e: any) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt write: --docs: ${e.message}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
    if (!docs.ok) { process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt write', docs.code, `${docs.message}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return docs.code === 'DOCS_AUDIT_BLOCKED' ? EXIT.refused : EXIT.fail; }
    const exceptionLine = docsExceptionLine(docs.docs);
    if (bodyFile && exceptionLine && !bodyText.split(/\r?\n/).some(l => l.trim() === exceptionLine)) {
      process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'DOCS_AUDIT_BLOCKED', `${bodyFile} does not carry the exception line verbatim: ${JSON.stringify(exceptionLine)}; nothing written`) + '\n');
      return EXIT.refused;
    }
  }
  let loopException: ReturnType<typeof parseReviewLoopException> | undefined;
  if (flag(rest, '--review-loop-exception') !== undefined) {
    const refuse = (why: string) => { process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'REVIEW_LOOP_EXCEPTION_INVALID', `${why}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; };
    try { loopException = parseReviewLoopException(jsonArg(flag(rest, '--review-loop-exception'))); } catch (e: any) { return refuse(`--review-loop-exception: ${e.message}`); }
    if (!loopException.ok) return refuse(loopException.message);
    let loop: unknown; try { loop = jsonArg(flag(rest, '--review-loop')); } catch {}
    const loopProblem = exceptionLoopProblem(loopException.exception, parseReviewLoop(loop));
    if (loopProblem) return refuse(`--review-loop-exception ${loopProblem}`);
    const fc = exceptionHead(loopException.exception);
    if (spawnSync('git', ['merge-base', '--is-ancestor', fc, head], { cwd: repoRoot }).status !== 0) return refuse(`${loopException.exception.fix_check ? 'fix_check' : 'second_pass'}.head ${fc.slice(0, 12)} is not ${head.slice(0, 12)} or an ancestor of it`);
    const line = reviewLoopExceptionLine(loopException.exception);
    if (bodyFile && !bodyText.split(/\r?\n/).some(l => l.trim() === line)) return refuse(`${bodyFile} does not carry the exception line verbatim: ${JSON.stringify(line)}`);
  }
  const leaked = securityFingerprints(bodyText);
  if (leaked.length) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${bodyFile} names security finding ${leaked.join(', ')}: a PR body is public, so a security finding appears only as the redacted line gstack-approvals rulings, dispositions or gstack-review-scope render prints, and its location and reason stay in the private record (docs/troubleshooting.md#security-finding-in-body); nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const ruledNotes = readRuledNotes(repoRoot);
  const unlisted = bodyFile ? ruledNotes.map(n => `Ruled note: ${ruledNoteText(n)}`).find(l => !bodyText.split(/\r?\n/).some(b => b.trim() === l)) : undefined;
  if (unlisted) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${bodyFile} does not list ruled note ${JSON.stringify(unlisted)} (gstack-approvals rulings prints each line the body carries); nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  let gateDispositions: ReturnType<typeof appliedGateDispositions>['applied'];
  try { gateDispositions = appliedGateDispositions(repoRoot, { pin: 'HEAD' }).applied; }
  catch (e: any) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `the owner gate dispositions at HEAD cannot be derived (${e.message}); the receipt always records them, so an unreadable approval store or a git error writes nothing`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  if (gateDispositions.length && !bodyFile) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `the approval store applies ${gateDispositions.length} owner gate disposition(s) at HEAD (${gateDispositions.map(d => d.approval).join(', ')}), so write needs --body <the PR body> carrying each "Gate disposition: …" line gstack-approvals dispositions prints; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const undisclosed = bodyFile ? gateDispositions.map(d => `Gate disposition: ${gateDispositionText(d)}`).find(l => !bodyText.split(/\r?\n/).some(b => b.trim() === l)) : undefined;
  if (undisclosed) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${bodyFile} does not list gate disposition ${JSON.stringify(undisclosed)} (gstack-approvals dispositions prints each line the body carries); nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const carried = ciCarried(base);
  const unlistedException = bodyFile ? laneExceptionBodyLines(carried).find(l => !bodyText.split(/\r?\n/).some(b => b.trim() === l)) : undefined;
  if (unlistedException) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${bodyFile} does not list ${JSON.stringify(unlistedException)} (accept's TEST_LANE_EXCEPTION: line; the body carries it as one line); nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const mechanical = readMechanicalLines(repoRoot, git(['rev-parse', `${head}^{tree}`], repoRoot) ?? '');
  const unlistedRetake = bodyFile ? mechanical.find(l => !bodyText.split(/\r?\n/).some(b => b.trim() === l)) : undefined;
  if (unlistedRetake) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${bodyFile} does not list ${JSON.stringify(unlistedRetake)} (finish's MECHANICAL: lines; the body carries each as one line); nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const declared = (flag(rest, '--declare-risk') ?? '').split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  if (rest.includes('--declare-risk') && (!declared.length || declared.some(c => !(RISK_CLASSES as readonly string[]).includes(c)))) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `--declare-risk ${flag(rest, '--declare-risk') ?? ''}: each class is one of ${RISK_CLASSES.join(', ')}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const review = receiptReviewAtHead(repoRoot, base, path.dirname(Bun.fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), headSha ?? head, declared as RiskClass[]);
  let reviewDepth = review.depth;
  const platformId = flag(rest, '--platform-review');
  if (platformId !== undefined) {
    const p = platformReceiptDepth(repoRoot, base, reviewDepth, headSha ?? head, platformId, flag(rest, '--pr'));
    if (!p.ok) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${p.message}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
    reviewDepth = p.depth;
  }
  if (review.exclude.state === 'refused') { for (const l of review.exclude.lines) process.stderr.write(`${l}; nothing written\n`); return EXIT.refused; }
  const excludeNow = review.exclude.state === 'active' ? review.exclude.record : null;
  const excludeGiven = flag(rest, '--review-exclude') ?? 'none';
  const excludeBound = writeExcludeBinds(repoRoot, base, headSha ?? head, review, flag(rest, '--review-exclude'), flag(rest, '--docs-post'), flag(rest, '--docs-pre'), flag(rest, '--docs-audit-read'));
  if (!excludeBound.ok && excludeBound.packet) {
    const at = headSha ?? head;
    const packet = path.resolve(repoRoot, git(['rev-parse', '--git-path', `gstack/docs-audit-read-${at.slice(0, 12)}.md`], repoRoot) ?? `.git/gstack/docs-audit-read-${at.slice(0, 12)}.md`);
    try { fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(packet), { recursive: true }); fs.writeFileSync(packet, excludeBound.packet.text); }
    catch (e) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt write: ${excludeBound.why}, but the reader's packet ${packet} cannot be written (${(e as Error).message.split('\n')[0]}); make its directory writable, then rerun write; nothing written\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
    process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_DOCS_AUDIT_READ', `${excludeBound.why}: one scoped reader (not a review round) reads ${packet}, then rerun write with --docs-audit-read <record.json> written outside the worktree ({"head":"${at}","paths":${JSON.stringify(excludeBound.packet.paths)},"reviewer":"<model>","verdict":"clean","packet_sha256":"${excludeBound.packet.sha256}"}); a finding goes to the lane's Captain; nothing written`) + '\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  if (!excludeBound.ok) {
    process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt write: field=review_exclude expected=${excludeNow?.digest ?? 'none'} recorded=${excludeGiven} source=${excludeNow?.source ?? `origin/${base} (no review_exclude_paths)`}: the --review-exclude argument names another selection than ${base}'s review_exclude_paths gives ${head.slice(0, 12)} (write compares the argument, not the review ledger)${flag(rest, '--review-exclude') === undefined ? '; no --review-exclude was given, so write compared none' : ''}${excludeBound.why ? `; the docs-audit exception does not apply: ${excludeBound.why}` : ''}; fix: when only Step 14.5's docs audit changed files under review_exclude_paths after the review, pass its --docs-post <audit-id>-post.json and --docs-pre <its Prepare snapshot>; otherwise rerun /ship's review on ${head.slice(0, 12)} (gstack-review-dispatch pass --base ${base}), run gstack-review-dispatch verify --ledger <ledger> and write with the --review-exclude <d> its REVIEW_EXCLUDE_RECORD: line prints (none when it prints no such line); nothing written (RECEIPT_INVALID)\n`);
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  if (excludeBound.line) process.stderr.write(excludeBound.line + '\n');
  const product = reviewedProduct(repoRoot, base, head, pregateFile);
  let targeted: ReturnType<typeof parseReviewTargeted> | undefined;
  if (flag(rest, '--review-targeted') !== undefined) {
    try { targeted = parseReviewTargeted(jsonArg(flag(rest, '--review-targeted')), product.product_patch_id ?? 'none', read => reviewedProduct(repoRoot, base, read, pregateFile).product_patch_id, read => targetedClassesSince(repoRoot, read, headSha ?? head, base, review.exclude.state === 'active' ? review.exclude.excluded : undefined), read => plainDocsSince(repoRoot, read, headSha ?? head, base), read => spawnSync('git', ['merge-base', '--is-ancestor', read, headSha ?? head], { cwd: repoRoot, timeout: 30_000 }).status === 0); } catch (e: any) { targeted = { ok: false, message: `--review-targeted: ${e.message}` }; }
  }
  if (targeted && !targeted.ok) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${targeted.message}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const approval = approvalForReceipt({ repoRoot, base, head, citationText: [bodyText, ...flags(rest, '--approval')].join('\n'), runDirs: flags(rest, '--approval-run') });
  if (approval.kind === 'invalid') {
    for (const line of approval.lines) process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'APPROVAL_CLASSES_INVALID', line) + '\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  if (approval.kind === 'error' && approval.code) { process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', approval.code, `${approval.message}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  if (approval.kind === 'error') { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt write: approval classes: ${approval.message}; nothing written\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  if (approval.kind === 'missing') {
    for (const m of approval.missing) process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'APPROVAL_CITATION_MISSING', `${m.class} (${m.token}; effects in ${m.files.join(', ')}): ${m.reasons.join('; ')}`) + '\n');
    process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt write: nothing written\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  if (approval.kind === 'ok' && approval.note) process.stderr.write(approval.note + '\n');
  let input: Partial<ShipReceipt> & { docs?: unknown };
  try {
    const issuesFile = jsonArg(flag(rest, '--issues'));
    const loopRaw = jsonArg(flag(rest, '--review-loop'));
    const reviewLoop = loopRaw ? parseReviewLoop(loopRaw) : undefined;
    if (loopRaw && !reviewLoop) throw new Error('--review-loop needs integer passes, blocking_found and deferred (gstack-review-scope summary --out <file>, then @<file>)');
    const ruledOpen = unruledOpenBlockers(loopRaw, ruledNotes, ruledHead => spawnSync('git', ['merge-base', '--is-ancestor', ruledHead, headSha ?? head], { cwd: repoRoot, timeout: 30_000 }).status === 0);
    const at = headSha ?? head, baseRef = `origin/${base.replace(/^origin\//, '')}`, run = flag(rest, '--run'), pr = Number(flag(rest, '--pr'));
    const blockers = (Array.isArray(loopRaw?.open) ? loopRaw.open : []).filter((b: any) => ruledOpen.includes(typeof b === 'string' ? b : b?.id));
    const rows = ruledOpen.length ? reviewRows(repoRoot) ?? [] : [];
    const grants = ruledOpen.length ? readReviewRoundGrants(repoRoot).filter(g => g.kind === 'fix-check' && grantForPr(g, pr)) : [];
    const live = grants.length && !receiptRuns(bodyText).length && flag(rest, '--pr') ? readBody(['--pr', flag(rest, '--pr')!, ...(flag(rest, '--repo') ? ['--repo', flag(rest, '--repo')!] : [])]) : undefined;
    const clearing = ruledOpen.length ? await import('../lib/fix-check-clearing') : undefined;
    const byGrant = !grants.length || !clearing ? undefined : !run ? { ids: [], why: 'write names no --run, so no run spent the grant' } : clearing.clearByGrant(repoRoot, { pr, run, head: at, baseRef, body: live?.ok ? live.body : bodyText, grants, rows, open: blockers });
    const byTrailer = clearing ? clearing.clearByTrailer(repoRoot, { head: at, baseRef, rows, open: blockers }) : [];
    if (byGrant) process.stderr.write(`FIX_CHECK_CLEAR: ${byGrant.ids.length ? `grant=${byGrant.approval} run=${byGrant.run} closed=${byGrant.ids.join(',')}` : 'none'}${byGrant.why ? ` (${byGrant.why})` : ''}\n`);
    for (const t of byTrailer) process.stderr.write(`TRAILER_CLEAR: ${t.id} (fixed by ${t.commit.slice(0, 12)}, read clean by the full review at ${t.review.slice(0, 12)})\n`);
    const open = ruledOpen.filter(id => !byGrant?.ids.includes(id) && !byTrailer.some(t => t.id === id));
    if (open.length) { process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_BLOCKER_OPEN', `${open.join(', ')}; nothing written`) + '\n'); return EXIT.refused; }
    input = {
      schema_version: 1, pr: flag(rest, '--pr') !== undefined ? Number(flag(rest, '--pr')) : undefined, head,
      version: flag(rest, '--version') ?? receiptVersion(repoRoot, head, base), base,
      gated_tree: flag(rest, '--gated-tree') ?? tree?.gated_tree, predecessor: flag(rest, '--predecessor') ?? tree?.predecessor?.recorded_head ?? undefined,
      tree: tree?.tree, gate_reuse: tree ? `${tree.gate_reuse} (${tree.gate_reuse_reason})` : undefined,
      gate: jsonArg(flag(rest, '--gate')), ci: jsonArg(flag(rest, '--ci')), ci_carried: carried,
      spend_usd: flag(rest, '--spend-usd') !== undefined ? (Number.isFinite(Number(flag(rest, '--spend-usd'))) ? Number(flag(rest, '--spend-usd')) : flag(rest, '--spend-usd')) : undefined,
      calls: callsArg(rest),
      session_kind: sessionKind, artifacts_consumed: flag(rest, '--artifacts-consumed'), run: flag(rest, '--run'), thread: flag(rest, '--thread'),
      policy: flag(rest, '--policy') ?? tree?.policy, queue_mode: flag(rest, '--queue-mode'), preregistration: flag(rest, '--preregistration'), history: flag(rest, '--history'),
      ...pregate, issues: issuesFile ? receiptIssuesFrom(issuesFile) : undefined, approval: approval.kind === 'ok' ? approval.approval : undefined,
      review_loop: reviewLoop, ...(docs?.ok ? { docs: docs.docs } : {}), ...product,
      gstack_version: installedGstackVersion(), review_depth: reviewDepth, review_loop_exception: loopException?.ok ? loopException.exception : undefined, review_round_grants: roundGrantsFor(repoRoot, flag(rest, '--pr'))?.map(g => publicRoundGrant(g, ruledNotes)), cleared_by_grant: byGrant?.ids.length ? { approval: byGrant.approval!, run: byGrant.run!, ids: byGrant.ids } : undefined, cleared_by_trailer: byTrailer.length ? byTrailer : undefined, ruled_notes: ruledNotes.length ? ruledNotes.map(publicRuledNote) : undefined, gate_dispositions: gateDispositions.map(publicGateDisposition), mechanical: mechanical.length ? mechanical : undefined, review_targeted: targeted?.ok ? targeted.targeted : undefined,
      design: review.frontend ? { mode: 'static', reason: 'no preview declared' } : undefined,
      base_red: pause ? receiptBaseRed(pause) : undefined,
      review_exclude: receiptExclude(review.exclude),
      review_exclude_fallback: receiptExcludeFallback(review.exclude),
      docs_audit_read: excludeBound.read,
      no_stop: noStopArg(flag(rest, '--no-stop')),
    };
  } catch (e: any) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt write: ${e.message}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  if (input.pr !== undefined && !Number.isInteger(input.pr)) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt write: --pr must be an integer\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const receipt = orderReceipt(input);
  const errors = validateReceipt(receipt);
  if (errors.length) {
    for (const e of errors) process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${e.message} at ${e.path}`) + '\n');
    process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt write: nothing written\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  const targetedVerdict = receiptTargetedAtHead(repoRoot, `origin/${base.replace(/^origin\//, '')}`, receipt, receipt.head);
  if (targetedVerdict.line.includes('(unchecked: ')) process.stderr.write(targetedVerdict.line + '\n');
  if (!targetedVerdict.ok) {
    process.stderr.write(`${targetedVerdict.line}\n${resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${targetedVerdict.message}; run the targeted reader on HEAD and pass its record (--review-targeted @<gstack-review-dispatch verify --targeted-out file>); nothing written`)}\n`);
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  const body = bodyFile;
  const missing = body && receipt.issues ? missingIssueLines(fs.existsSync(body) ? fs.readFileSync(body, 'utf8') : '', receipt.issues) : [];
  if (missing.length) {
    process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt write', 'ISSUE_LINKS_MISSING', `${body} lacks ${missing.map(l => JSON.stringify(l)).join(', ')}`) + '\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  const block = renderReceiptBlock(receipt);
  const out = flag(rest, '--out');
  if (out) fs.writeFileSync(out, block);
  const closed = [...(receipt.cleared_by_grant ? [`Closed by grant ${receipt.cleared_by_grant.approval}: ${receipt.cleared_by_grant.ids.join(', ')} (the granted fix-check of run ${receipt.cleared_by_grant.run} read the fix clean)`] : []),
    ...(receipt.cleared_by_trailer ?? []).map(t => `Closed by fix ${t.commit.slice(0, 12)}: ${t.id} (a later full review at ${t.review.slice(0, 12)} read it clean)`)];
  if (body) {
    let text = fs.existsSync(body) ? fs.readFileSync(body, 'utf8') : '';
    const pr = flag(rest, '--pr');
    if (pr && fs.existsSync(body) && !extractReceipt(text).found && !receiptRuns(text).length) {
      const live = readBody(['--pr', pr, ...(flag(rest, '--repo') ? ['--repo', flag(rest, '--repo')!] : [])]);
      const prior = live.ok ? extractReceipt(live.body).receipt : undefined;
      const runs = live.ok ? receiptRuns(live.body) : [];
      if (!live.ok) process.stderr.write(`RECEIPT_RUNS: PR #${pr}'s earlier runs were not read (${live.why}), so ${body} keeps only this run; fix: ${live.fix}\n`);
      else if (prior || runs.length) text = withAgentNotes(text, [(splitAgentNotes(text).notes ?? '').trim(), prior ? renderReceiptBlock(prior) : '', runs.length ? '```' + RUNS_FENCE + '\n' + runs.map(r => JSON.stringify(r)).join('\n') + '\n```\n' : ''].filter(Boolean).join('\n\n'));
    }
    const notes = splitAgentNotes(text).notes ?? '';
    const lines = closed.filter(l => !notes.includes(l));
    fs.writeFileSync(body, placeReceipt(lines.length ? withAgentNotes(text, [notes.trim(), ...lines].filter(Boolean).join('\n\n')) : text, receipt));
  }
  process.stderr.write(receiptSummaryLine(receipt) + '\n');
  process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify(receipt) + '\n' : block);
  return EXIT.ok;
}

/** The branch's review-log rows as gstack-review-read prints them, or null when it fails. */
function reviewRows(repoRoot: string): Record<string, any>[] | null {
  const log = runScriptSync(path.join(path.dirname(Bun.fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), 'gstack-review-read'), [], { cwd: repoRoot, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 60_000, maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024 });
  return log.status !== 0 ? null : (log.stdout ?? '').split('\n---CONFIG---')[0]!.split('\n').flatMap(l => { try { const v = JSON.parse(l); return v && typeof v === 'object' ? [v] : []; } catch { return []; } });
}

function cmdRead(rest: string[], json: boolean): number {
  const bodyFile = flag(rest, '--body');
  const pr = flag(rest, '--pr');
  let body: string;
  if (bodyFile) body = fs.readFileSync(bodyFile, 'utf8');
  else if (pr) {
    const repo = flag(rest, '--repo');
    const r = gh(['pr', 'view', pr, ...(repo ? ['--repo', repo] : []), '--json', 'body']);
    if (!r.ok) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt read: gh pr view failed: ${r.err}\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
    try { body = JSON.parse(r.out).body ?? ''; } catch { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt read: gh returned no JSON body\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  } else { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt read: --pr <n> or --body <file> is required\n${HELP}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  const ex = extractReceipt(body);
  if (!ex.found) {
    process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt read', 'RECEIPT_MISSING', pr ? `PR #${pr}` : bodyFile!) + '\n');
    if (json) process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ found: false, errors: [] }) + '\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  if (ex.errors.length) {
    for (const e of ex.errors) process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt read', 'RECEIPT_INVALID', `${e.message} at ${e.path}`) + '\n');
    if (json) process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ found: true, valid: false, errors: ex.errors, raw: ex.raw }) + '\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  process.stderr.write(receiptSummaryLine(ex.receipt!) + '\n');
  if (rest.includes('--check-prose')) {
    const prose = checkReceiptProse(ex.receipt as unknown as Record<string, unknown>, body);
    process.stderr.write(proseLine(prose) + '\n');
    if (prose.mismatches.length) {
      process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt read', 'RECEIPT_PROSE_MISMATCH', prose.mismatches.map(m => `${m.field} body=${m.prose} receipt=${m.receipt}`).join(', ')) + '\n');
      if (json) process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ found: true, valid: true, receipt: ex.receipt, prose }) + '\n');
      return EXIT.fail;
    }
    if (json) { process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ found: true, valid: true, receipt: ex.receipt, prose }) + '\n'); return EXIT.ok; }
  }
  process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify(ex.receipt) + '\n' : renderReceiptBlock(ex.receipt!));
  return EXIT.ok;
}

/**
 * /ship's terminal line (docs/unattended.md#the-terminal-line). The receipt in
 * the PR body (or the handoff file) must bind to HEAD: then the run record
 * goes under <state>/ship/runs/ with the head, the PR and the receipt, and
 * the last stdout line is GSTACK_RESULT: skill=ship status=complete head=<sha> run=<dir>.
 * A missing or stale receipt is status=refused run=- (exit 3), so a parent
 * never has to parse the PR body to know whether /ship finished at this head.
 */
function cmdResult(rest: string[], json: boolean): number {
  const bodyFile = flag(rest, '--body');
  const prFlag = flag(rest, '--pr');
  if (prFlag !== undefined && !/^[1-9]\d*$/.test(prFlag)) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt result: --pr must be a PR number, got ${JSON.stringify(prFlag.slice(0, 40))}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  const pr = prFlag;
  if (prFlag !== undefined && flag(rest, '--body') !== undefined) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt result: pass --pr <n> (the PR body, checked against its pushed head) or --body <file> (the handoff receipt), not both\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);
  const head = (flag(rest, '--head') ?? (repoRoot ? git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], repoRoot) : undefined))?.toLowerCase();
  const refused = (code: 'QUEUE_RECEIPT_MISSING' | 'QUEUE_RECEIPT_STALE', message: string) => {
    process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt result', code, message) + '\n');
    process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ skill: 'ship', status: 'refused', run: '-', code, message }) + '\n' : 'GSTACK_RESULT: skill=ship status=refused run=-\n');
    return EXIT.refused;
  };
  if (!head) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt result: --head <sha> is required outside a git repository\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  if (!/^[0-9a-f]{40,64}$/i.test(head)) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt result: --head must be a full hex commit id, got ${JSON.stringify(head.slice(0, 40))}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  const incomplete = (why: string) => {
    process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt result: ${why}\n`);
    process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ skill: 'ship', status: 'incomplete', run: '-', message: why }) + '\n' : 'GSTACK_RESULT: skill=ship status=incomplete run=-\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  };
  let body: string;
  let source: string;
  if (bodyFile) {
    if (!fs.existsSync(bodyFile)) return refused('QUEUE_RECEIPT_MISSING', `${bodyFile} does not exist; /ship did not write its receipt`);
    try { body = fs.readFileSync(bodyFile, 'utf8'); } catch (e) { return incomplete(`cannot read ${bodyFile}: ${e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e)}`); }
    source = path.resolve(bodyFile);
  } else if (pr) {
    const repo = flag(rest, '--repo');
    const r = gh(['pr', 'view', pr, ...(repo ? ['--repo', repo] : []), '--json', 'body,headRefOid']);
    if (!r.ok) return incomplete(`gh pr view failed: ${r.err.trim()}`);
    let pushed: unknown;
    try { const v = JSON.parse(r.out); body = v.body ?? ''; pushed = v.headRefOid; } catch { return incomplete('gh returned no JSON body'); }
    if (typeof pushed !== 'string' || !/^[0-9a-f]{12,64}$/i.test(pushed)) return incomplete(`gh pr view returned no headRefOid for PR #${pr}`);
    if (!pushed.toLowerCase().startsWith(head.toLowerCase())) {
      return refused('QUEUE_RECEIPT_STALE', `HEAD ${head.slice(0, 12)} is not PR #${pr}'s pushed head ${pushed.slice(0, 12)}; push it, then rerun gstack-ship-receipt result`);
    }
    source = `PR #${pr}${repo ? ` (${repo})` : ''}`;
  } else { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt result: --pr <n> or --body <file> is required\n${HELP}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  const bound = bindReceipt(body, pr, [head], { conditional: true });
  if (!bound.ok) return refused(bound.code, bound.message);
  const red = bound.receipt.base_red;
  if (red) process.stderr.write(`SHIP_PAUSED: base-red cases=${red.cases.length} base=${red.base.slice(0, 12)} lane=${red.lane} expires=${red.expires_at}; gstack-base-red wait --pause <file>, then /ship --resume <record>\n`);
  return writeRunRecord({ receipt: bound.receipt, head, pr, source, repoRoot, out: flag(rest, '--out'), json, line: bound.line, incomplete, status: red ? 'incomplete' : 'complete' });
}

/** The run record under <state>/ship/runs/ and the terminal line, shared by `result` and `carry`. */
function writeRunRecord(a: { receipt: ShipReceipt; head: string; pr: string | undefined; source: string; repoRoot: string | undefined; out: string | undefined; json: boolean; line: string; incomplete: (why: string) => number; extra?: Record<string, unknown>; status?: 'complete' | 'incomplete' }): number {
  const status = a.status ?? 'complete';
  const stamp = new Date().toISOString().replace(/[:.]/g, '-');
  const dir = a.out ? path.resolve(a.out) : path.join(resolveStateRoot(), 'ship', 'runs', `${stamp}-${a.head.slice(0, 12)}`);
  const receiptPath = path.join(dir, 'ship-receipt.md');
  try {
    fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });
    fs.writeFileSync(receiptPath, renderReceiptBlock(a.receipt));
  } catch (e) { return a.incomplete(`cannot write the run record under ${dir}: ${e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e)}`); }
  const run = {
    schema_version: 1, skill: 'ship', status, head: a.head, pr: a.receipt.pr ?? (a.pr ? Number(a.pr) : null), base: a.receipt.base, version: a.receipt.version ?? null,
    queue_mode: a.receipt.queue_mode ?? null, session_kind: a.receipt.session_kind ?? process.env.GSTACK_SESSION_KIND ?? null,
    receipt: receiptPath, receipt_source: a.source, branch: a.repoRoot ? git(['rev-parse', '--abbrev-ref', 'HEAD'], a.repoRoot) ?? null : null, created_at: new Date().toISOString(),
    ...(a.extra ?? {}),
  };
  try { fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, 'ship-run.json'), JSON.stringify(run, null, 2) + '\n'); } catch (e) { return a.incomplete(`cannot write ${path.join(dir, 'ship-run.json')}: ${e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e)}`); }
  process.stderr.write(a.line + '\n');
  process.stdout.write(a.json ? JSON.stringify({ ...run, run: dir }) + '\n' : `GSTACK_RESULT: skill=ship status=${status} head=${a.head} run=${dir}\n`);
  return status === 'complete' ? EXIT.ok : EXIT.fail;
}

/** `git patch-id --verbatim` exists from git 2.39 (docs/ship-policy.md#receipt-carry); an older git is a named refusal, never a silent fallback to the whitespace-stripping default. */
const CARRY_MIN_GIT = '2.39';
function gitVersionBelow(repoRoot: string, minimum: string): string | null {
  const raw = git(['--version'], repoRoot) ?? '';
  const m = /(\d+)\.(\d+)(?:\.(\d+))?/.exec(raw);
  if (!m) return raw || 'unknown';
  const [minMajor, minMinor] = minimum.split('.').map(Number) as [number, number];
  const major = Number(m[1]); const minor = Number(m[2]);
  return major > minMajor || (major === minMajor && minor >= minMinor) ? null : m[0];
}

type PregateField = { pregate: string; requires_remote?: string[]; flaky_exception?: ShipReceipt['flaky_exception'] };
/** A pregate result file → the receipt's pregate field, verified current for this checkout's tree (shared by write and carry). */
function pregateFieldFor(repoRoot: string, file: string, head: string, base?: string): { ok: true; field: PregateField } | { ok: false; errors: Array<{ code: string; message: string }> } {
  const read = readPregateFile(file);
  if (!read.file) return { ok: false, errors: read.errors.map(e => ({ code: e.code, message: `${e.message} at ${e.path}` })) };
  const v = verifyPregate(repoRoot, read.file, undefined, base);
  if (!v.ok) return { ok: false, errors: [{ code: v.code!, message: v.message ?? 'pregate is not current' }] };
  const foreign = exceptionConsumerProblem(read.file, head);
  if (foreign) return { ok: false, errors: [{ code: 'PREGATE_REMOTE_UNCLEARED', message: foreign }] };
  const remote = read.file.requires_remote ?? [];
  const exceptions = read.file.exceptions ?? [];
  return { ok: true, field: { pregate: `${read.file.verdict ?? 'pass'} @${read.file.tree.slice(0, 12)} (${read.file.checks.length} checks, current for ${head.slice(0, 12)})`, requires_remote: remote.length ? remote.map(r => `${r.lane}: ${r.receipt}`) : undefined, flaky_exception: exceptions.length ? exceptions.map(e => ({ lane: e.lane, runs: e.runs, cases: e.cases, grant: e.grant, by: e.by })) : undefined } };
}

/**
 * The receipt follows HEAD when the reviewed product is unchanged
 * (docs/unattended.md#the-terminal-line; harness lane E row 3). Four Captains
 * reran a full /ship on identical product code after a base merge or a
 * test-only fix; the carry compares the product diff against the base at the
 * receipt's head and at HEAD by patch-id, classifies every changed path, and
 * records the range-diff as evidence in the receipt it rewrites. After a rebase
 * or force-push it carries only onto a tree the receipt covers whose product
 * patch-id against the current base is the recorded one (planTreeCarry).
 */
function cmdCarry(rest: string[], json: boolean): number {
  const bodyFile = flag(rest, '--body');
  const pr = flag(rest, '--pr');
  if (pr !== undefined && !/^[1-9]\d*$/.test(pr)) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt carry: --pr must be a PR number, got ${JSON.stringify(pr.slice(0, 40))}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  if ((pr === undefined) === (bodyFile === undefined)) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt carry: pass --pr <n> or --body <file>, not both\n${HELP}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);
  if (!repoRoot) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt carry: run it inside the git checkout whose head carries the receipt\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  if (rest.includes('--recheck')) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt carry: --recheck is gone: a scoped re-check is advice only and never carries a receipt (GST-2673); run /ship on HEAD for the merge head\'s full review (docs/review-policy.md#rounds-per-pull-request)\n'); return EXIT.refused; }
  const head = (flag(rest, '--head') ?? git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], repoRoot))?.toLowerCase();
  if (!head || !/^[0-9a-f]{40,64}$/.test(head)) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt carry: cannot resolve HEAD\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const refused = (code: 'QUEUE_RECEIPT_MISSING' | 'QUEUE_RECEIPT_CONDITIONAL' | 'RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED' | 'RECEIPT_CARRY_PRODUCT_CHANGED' | 'RECEIPT_CARRY_SCOPED_REVIEW' | 'RECEIPT_CARRY_TREE_MISMATCH' | 'RECEIPT_GIT_TOO_OLD' | 'RECEIPT_CARRY_PREGATE_STALE', message: string) => {
    process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt carry', code, message) + '\n');
    process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ skill: 'ship', status: 'refused', run: '-', code, message }) + '\n' : `CARRY: refused (${code})\nGSTACK_RESULT: skill=ship status=refused run=-\n`);
    return EXIT.refused;
  };
  const incomplete = (why: string) => {
    process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt carry: ${why}\n`);
    process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ skill: 'ship', status: 'incomplete', run: '-', message: why }) + '\n' : 'GSTACK_RESULT: skill=ship status=incomplete run=-\n');
    return EXIT.fail;
  };
  const repo = flag(rest, '--repo');
  let body: string;
  let source: string;
  if (bodyFile) {
    if (!fs.existsSync(bodyFile)) return refused('QUEUE_RECEIPT_MISSING', `${bodyFile} does not exist`);
    body = fs.readFileSync(bodyFile, 'utf8');
    source = path.resolve(bodyFile);
  } else {
    const r = gh(['pr', 'view', pr!, ...(repo ? ['--repo', repo] : []), '--json', 'body,headRefOid']);
    if (!r.ok) return incomplete(`gh pr view failed: ${r.err}`);
    let pushed: unknown;
    try { const v = JSON.parse(r.out); body = v.body ?? ''; pushed = v.headRefOid; } catch { return incomplete('gh returned no JSON body'); }
    if (typeof pushed === 'string' && /^[0-9a-f]{12,64}$/i.test(pushed) && !pushed.toLowerCase().startsWith(head)) {
      return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `HEAD ${head.slice(0, 12)} is not PR #${pr}'s pushed head ${pushed.slice(0, 12)}; push first, then carry`);
    }
    source = `PR #${pr}${repo ? ` (${repo})` : ''}`;
  }
  const ex = extractReceipt(body);
  if (!ex.found) return refused('QUEUE_RECEIPT_MISSING', `${source} carries no ship receipt; run /ship`);
  if (!ex.receipt || ex.errors.length) return refused('QUEUE_RECEIPT_MISSING', `${source}'s ship receipt is invalid (${ex.errors[0]?.message ?? 'invalid'}); run /ship`);
  const receipt = ex.receipt;
  if (pr !== undefined && receipt.pr !== undefined && String(receipt.pr) !== pr) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the receipt names pr=${receipt.pr}, not this PR`);
  if (receipt.base_red) return refused('QUEUE_RECEIPT_CONDITIONAL', 'the receipt is paused on a red base, so there is nothing passing to carry; /ship --resume <record> re-runs Step 5 and writes a full receipt');
  const from = receipt.head.toLowerCase();
  if (!/^[0-9a-f]{40,64}$/.test(from)) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the receipt's head ${receipt.head.slice(0, 12)} is not a full commit id`);
  if (recheckCarried(receipt)) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the receipt reached ${from.slice(0, 12)} through a scoped re-check (carry: ${receipt.carry!.reason.slice(0, 160)}), which is advice only (GST-2673), so the product code it covered never got a full review; the receipt is unchanged: run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)} for the merge head's full review (docs/review-policy.md#rounds-per-pull-request)`);
  if (from === head) {
    process.stderr.write(receiptSummaryLine(receipt) + '\n');
    process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ skill: 'ship', status: 'current', head, carry: null }) + '\n' : `CARRY: current (the receipt already names ${head.slice(0, 12)})\n`);
    return EXIT.ok;
  }
  const oldGit = gitVersionBelow(repoRoot, CARRY_MIN_GIT);
  if (oldGit) return refused('RECEIPT_GIT_TOO_OLD', `git ${oldGit} cannot run patch-id --verbatim; the carry needs git ${CARRY_MIN_GIT} or later`);
  // The carry binds HEAD alone: pending edits are not in the commits it compares, and a parent that stops at CARRY: carried would report them shipped.
  const status = spawnSync('git', ['status', '--porcelain', '--untracked-files=all'], { cwd: repoRoot, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 30_000, maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });
  if (status.status !== 0) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', 'git status failed; the carry needs a readable working tree');
  const dirty = status.stdout.split('\n').filter(Boolean).map(l => l.slice(3).replace(/^.* -> /, ''));
  if (dirty.length) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the working tree has uncommitted changes (${dirty.slice(0, 5).join(', ')}${dirty.length > 5 ? ` +${dirty.length - 5} more` : ''}); commit them and carry at the new head, or run /ship`);
  const fromKnown = git(['cat-file', '-e', `${from}^{commit}`], repoRoot) !== undefined;
  const ancestor = fromKnown && spawnSync('git', ['merge-base', '--is-ancestor', from, head], { cwd: repoRoot, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 30_000 }).status === 0;
  const fromTree = fromKnown ? git(['rev-parse', `${from}^{tree}`], repoRoot) : undefined;
  const covered = [...(receipt.head_tree ? [receipt.head_tree] : fromTree ? [fromTree] : []), ...(receipt.carry?.trees ?? [])];
  if (!ancestor && !covered.length) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the receipt's head ${from.slice(0, 12)} is not an ancestor of HEAD ${head.slice(0, 12)} (rebased or force-pushed), and the receipt records no tree to compare; merge the base in next time, and run /ship now`);
  const base = flag(rest, '--base') ?? receipt.base ?? resolveBaseBranch(repoRoot);
  const baseRef = `origin/${base.replace(/^origin\//, '')}`;
  const headBase = git(['merge-base', baseRef, head], repoRoot);
  if (!headBase) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `cannot resolve the merge base of ${baseRef} (fetch it first)`);
  const rules = productRules(repoRoot, base, verifiedOutputs(repoRoot, base, flag(rest, '--pregate')));
  const headTree = git(['rev-parse', `${head}^{tree}`], repoRoot);
  if (!headTree) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `git could not read the tree of HEAD ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
  const headPatch = productPatchAgainstBase(repoRoot, rules, baseRef, head);
  if (typeof headPatch !== 'string') return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `git could not compute HEAD's product patch-id: ${headPatch.error}`);
  const reviewedBase = receipt.base.replace(/^origin\//, '');
  const retarget = reviewedBase !== base.replace(/^origin\//, '');
  let plan: ReturnType<typeof planCarry>;
  let scopedDryRun: string | undefined;
  if (!ancestor) {
    // Rewritten history: the receipt follows only onto a tree it already covers, with the product diff it recorded.
    const recorded = receipt.product_patch_id !== undefined ? (receipt.product_patch_id === 'none' ? '' : receipt.product_patch_id) : fromKnown ? productPatchAgainstBase(repoRoot, rules, baseRef, from) : { error: 'the receipt records no product patch-id and its head is not in this clone' };
    if (typeof recorded !== 'string') return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the reviewed product patch-id is unavailable: ${recorded.error}; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
    plan = planTreeCarry({ from, head, headTree, coveredTrees: covered, productPatchId: { recorded, head: headPatch } });
  } else {
    const fromBase = git(['merge-base', baseRef, from], repoRoot);
    if (!fromBase) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `cannot resolve the merge base of ${baseRef} (fetch it first)`);
    // The reviewed range runs from the fork point, or from a stack parent inside it that has since landed on the base: a
    // receipt written against the base while stacked reviewed the parent's hunks too, and the squash moved them into the
    // base (GST-1199). A parent counts only when merging it into the current base changes no product path.
    const measure = (rangeBase: string) => {
      const listed = [touchedPaths(repoRoot, rangeBase, from), touchedPaths(repoRoot, headBase, head), rangeBase === fromBase ? new Set<string>() : touchedPaths(repoRoot, fromBase, from)];
      if (!listed[0] || !listed[1] || !listed[2]) return `git could not list the paths the branch touched against ${base}; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`;
      // From a stack parent, a path whose reviewed content is the base's (an earlier base merge brought it in) is base
      // context, not reviewed product, unless HEAD changed it against the base (GST-1214).
      // A pathspec also names everything beneath a path, so a path with any compared path under it (a file the base turned
      // into a directory) stays in.
      const compared = [...listed[0], ...listed[1]];
      const baseMerged = rangeBase === fromBase ? [] : [...listed[0]].filter(p => !listed[2]!.has(p) && !listed[1]!.has(p) && !compared.some(q => q.startsWith(`${p}/`)));
      const touched = new Set([...listed[0], ...listed[1]].filter(p => !baseMerged.includes(p)));
      const found = productSpec(repoRoot, rules, from, head, { touched, sides: [[rangeBase, from], [headBase, head]], own: branchSides(repoRoot, baseRef, from, '') });
      if (!found) return `git diff ${from.slice(0, 12)} ${head.slice(0, 12)} failed`;
      const skip = baseMerged.map(p => `:(exclude,literal)${p}`);
      const spec = { ...found, product: [...found.product, ...skip], tests: [...found.tests, ...skip] };
      const ids = [patchId(repoRoot, rangeBase, from, spec.product), patchId(repoRoot, headBase, head, spec.product)];
      for (const r of ids) if (typeof r !== 'string') return `git could not compute the product patch-id at one of the heads: ${r.error}`;
      return { rangeBase, touched, spec, productFrom: ids[0] as string, productHead: ids[1] as string };
    };
    let measured = measure(fromBase);
    if (typeof measured === 'string') return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', measured);
    const stackParent = !retarget && measured.productFrom !== measured.productHead ? landedStackParent(repoRoot, { rangeBase: fromBase, reviewed: from, currentBase: headBase }, measured.spec.product) : null;
    if (stackParent) measured = measure(stackParent);
    if (typeof measured === 'string') return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', measured);
    const { rangeBase, touched, spec, productFrom, productHead } = measured;
    const { changed } = spec;
    const asId = (r: string | { error: string }) => (typeof r === 'string' ? r : '');
    const testFrom = asId(patchId(repoRoot, rangeBase, from, spec.tests));
    const testHead = asId(patchId(repoRoot, headBase, head, spec.tests));
    // A stacked child whose parent landed on the base (#3570): the receipt reviewed the child's own range against the
    // parent branch, and the PR now targets the base. That reviewed range (the recorded product patch-id, else the one
    // against origin/<receipt base> when it still resolves) must be HEAD's whole product diff against the base, computed
    // the way write records it (headPatch): the parent fully landed and the child is unchanged. Anything else fails closed.
    let reviewed = productFrom;
    if (retarget) {
      const parentRef = `origin/${reviewedBase}`;
      const recorded = receipt.product_patch_id !== undefined ? (receipt.product_patch_id === 'none' ? '' : receipt.product_patch_id)
        : git(['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', `${parentRef}^{commit}`], repoRoot) ? productPatchAgainstBase(repoRoot, rules, parentRef, from) : { error: `the receipt records no product patch-id and ${parentRef} no longer resolves` };
      if (typeof recorded !== 'string') return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the receipt was reviewed against ${reviewedBase}, not ${base}, and its reviewed product diff is unavailable: ${recorded.error}; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
      reviewed = recorded;
    }
    const current = retarget ? headPatch : productHead;
    const changedProduct: string[] = [];
    let walkCut = false;
    const contextPaths: string[] = [];
    const stampOnly: string[] = [];
    if (retarget && reviewed !== current) changedProduct.push(`HEAD's product diff against ${base} is not the one reviewed against ${reviewedBase} (the parent has not fully landed on ${base}, or the branch changed since)`);
    else if (productFrom !== productHead && !retarget) {
      // planCarry names at most CARRY_NAMED_PATHS differing paths, so the walk stops there, and it reads only the paths the
      // branch itself touched against the base at either head: a base merge brings in every path the base changed, none of
      // which can differ between the two base diffs. A touched path with the same blob at both heads and at both bases has
      // the same patch, so only paths that moved on one side are compared (GST-448: 6000 touched paths). A path whose only difference is base context next to unchanged hunks
      // (lib/ship-patch.ts) needs a scoped review instead of the loop.
      const sides = { reviewedBase: rangeBase, reviewed: from, currentBase: headBase, current: head };
      const moved = [touchedPaths(repoRoot, from, head), touchedPaths(repoRoot, rangeBase, headBase)];
      if (moved.some(l => !l)) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `git could not list the paths the branch touched against ${base}; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
      const [movedHead, movedBase] = moved as Set<string>[];
      // A stamp file the branch changed as product (its own row) whose reviewed-to-current change is a stamp on its own lines
      // and that the base did not touch holds no unreviewed change, so the comparison leaves its bytes out (GST-980).
      for (const p of [...touched].filter(p => movedHead.has(p) || movedBase.has(p)).sort()) {
        if (changedProduct.length >= CARRY_NAMED_PATHS) { walkCut = true; break; }
        const cls = changed.find(c => c.path === p)?.class ?? classifyCarryPath(p, rules.extra);
        if (cls === 'metadata' && spec.ownRows.includes(p) && !movedBase.has(p)) stampOnly.push(p);
        if (cls === 'metadata' && spec.demoted.includes(p) && movedBase.has(p) && /(^|\/)package\.json$/.test(p)) {
          const masked = Object.values(sides).map(ref => {
            const r = spawnSync('git', ['show', `${ref}:${p}`], { cwd: repoRoot, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 30_000, maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });
            try { const { version: _, ...rest } = JSON.parse(r.status === 0 ? r.stdout : 'null') ?? {}; return JSON.stringify(rest); } catch { return null; }
          });
          const [rb, rv, cb, cv] = masked;
          if (masked.some(m => m === null) || rv !== cv || rb !== cb) changedProduct.push(p);
          else stampOnly.push(p);
          continue;
        }
        if (cls !== 'product') continue;
        const verdict = comparePath(repoRoot, sides, p);
        if (verdict === 'changed') changedProduct.push(p);
        else if (verdict === 'context') contextPaths.push(p);
      }
      const left = [...contextPaths, ...stampOnly];
      if (!changedProduct.length && !left.length) changedProduct.push('(a product path outside the branch\'s touched files; compare the two base diffs)');
      else if (!changedProduct.length) {
        const rest = [...spec.product, ...left.map(p => `:(exclude,literal)${p}`)];
        const restFrom = patchId(repoRoot, rangeBase, from, rest);
        const restHead = patchId(repoRoot, headBase, head, rest);
        if (typeof restFrom !== 'string' || typeof restHead !== 'string' || restFrom !== restHead) changedProduct.push(`(a product path outside ${left.join(', ')}; compare the two base diffs without them)`);
      }
    }
    const stampedRows = changedProduct.length ? [] : stampOnly;
    let scopedReview: string | undefined;
    const packetBody = !changedProduct.length && contextPaths.length ? contextPacket(repoRoot, { reviewedBase: rangeBase, reviewed: from, currentBase: headBase, current: head }, contextPaths) : null;
    if (packetBody?.over.length) changedProduct.push(...packetBody.over.map(p => `${p} (too large for the scoped review: over ${PACKET_SECTION_CAP} lines in a section)`));
    if (packetBody && !changedProduct.length) {
      const record = flag(rest, '--scoped-review');
      if (!record && rest.includes('--dry-run')) {
        scopedDryRun = `base context moved next to the reviewed hunks in ${contextPaths.join(', ')}: carry without --dry-run writes the scoped-review packet for one fix-check reviewer, then carry --scoped-review <record.json>; nothing written`;
        scopedReview = `base context moved (scoped review pending: ${contextPaths.join(', ')})`;
      } else if (!record) {
        const gitPath = git(['rev-parse', '--git-path', `gstack/scoped-review-${head.slice(0, 12)}.md`], repoRoot);
        const packet = path.resolve(repoRoot, gitPath ?? `.git/gstack/scoped-review-${head.slice(0, 12)}.md`);
        try {
          fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(packet), { recursive: true });
          fs.writeFileSync(packet, packetBody.text);
        } catch (e) {
          return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `base context moved next to the reviewed hunks in ${contextPaths.join(', ')}, but the scoped-review packet ${packet} cannot be written (${(e as Error).message.split('\n')[0]}); make its directory writable, then rerun carry`);
        }
        return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_SCOPED_REVIEW', `base context moved next to the reviewed hunks in ${contextPaths.join(', ')}: one fix-check reviewer reads ${packet}, then rerun carry with --scoped-review <record.json> ({"head":"${head}","paths":[…],"reviewer":"<model>","verdict":"clean"}); a blocking finding means /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
      }
      if (record) {
        const review = readScopedReview(record, { head }, contextPaths);
        if (!review.ok) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `--scoped-review: ${review.message}`);
        scopedReview = `base context moved (scoped review by ${review.review.reviewer}: ${contextPaths.join(', ')})`;
      }
    }
    const mergeCommits = (git(['rev-list', '--merges', '--count', `${from}..${head}`], repoRoot) ?? '0').trim();
    // Evidence for the record, never the decision: a slow range-diff is reported unavailable rather than waited for.
    const rangeRaw = spawnSync('git', ['range-diff', '--no-color', `${rangeBase}..${from}`, `${headBase}..${head}`], { cwd: repoRoot, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 15_000, maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024 });
    const rangeDiff = rangeRaw.status === 0 ? (rangeRaw.stdout.trim().split('\n').slice(0, 20).join('\n') || '(empty: identical ranges)') : `unavailable: ${(rangeRaw.stderr ?? '').trim().split('\n')[0] || (rangeRaw.signal ? `range-diff killed by ${rangeRaw.signal} after 15 s` : 'range-diff failed')}`;
    // J1: a bounded product change since the reviewed head gets an advisory packet for one reader; it never carries (crew/lib/ship-recheck.ts, GST-2673).
    if (changedProduct.length) {
      const named = changedProduct.filter(p => !p.startsWith('(') && !p.includes(' ('));
      const inter = named.length ? spawnSync('git', ['diff', '--no-color', '--no-ext-diff', from, head, '--', ...named.map(p => `:(literal)${p}`)], { cwd: repoRoot, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 30_000, maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024 }) : null;
      const fullRange = rangeRaw.status === 0 && inter?.status === 0 ? `${rangeRaw.stdout.trim()}\n${inter.stdout.trim()}` : null;
      const numstat = named.length ? spawnSync('git', ['diff', '--numstat', from, head, '--', ...named.map(p => `:(literal)${p}`)], { cwd: repoRoot, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 30_000, maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 }) : null;
      const binary = numstat?.status !== 0 || (numstat?.stdout ?? '').split('\n').some(l => l.startsWith('-\t-\t'));
      // Moved base context composes into the same packet, bound to range_base (GST-1561).
      const context = contextPaths.length ? contextPacket(repoRoot, { reviewedBase: rangeBase, reviewed: from, currentBase: headBase, current: head }, contextPaths) : undefined;
      const bound = context ? { rangeBase, context: context.text } : {};
      const r = planRecheck({ code: 'RECEIPT_CARRY_PRODUCT_CHANGED', ancestor, retarget, rangeDiff: fullRange, unnamedPaths: named.length !== changedProduct.length, legacy: !receipt.review_depth, walkCut, contextPaths: contextPaths.length, context, binary });
      if (!r.ok) process.stderr.write(`RECHECK: not eligible (${r.reason}); run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}\n`);
      else {
        let where = 'not written (dry run)';
        if (!rest.includes('--dry-run')) {
          const packet = path.resolve(repoRoot, git(['rev-parse', '--git-path', `gstack/recheck-${head.slice(0, 12)}.md`], repoRoot) ?? `.git/gstack/recheck-${head.slice(0, 12)}.md`);
          try { fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(packet), { recursive: true }); fs.writeFileSync(packet, recheckPacket({ from, head, plan: r, rangeDiff: fullRange!, ...bound })); where = packet; }
          catch (e) { where = `unwritable: ${(e as Error).message.split('\n')[0]}`; }
        }
        process.stderr.write(`RECHECK: advisory range_diff_lines=${r.lines} range_diff_sha256=${r.sha256} packet=${where}; one reader may read it for advice, but it never carries the receipt (GST-2673): run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)} for the merge head's full review (docs/review-policy.md#rounds-per-pull-request)\n`);
      }
    }
    plan = planCarry({ from, head, changed, productPatchId: { from: reviewed as string, head: current as string }, testPatchId: { from: testFrom, head: testHead }, changedProduct, mergeCommits: Number(mergeCommits) || 0, rangeDiff, ...(retarget ? { retargetedFrom: reviewedBase } : {}), ...(stackParent ? { stackParent } : {}), ...(scopedReview ? { scopedReview } : {}), ...(stampedRows.length ? { stampedRows } : {}) });
  }
  if (!plan.ok) return refused(plan.code, plan.message);
  // Eligibility is not publication: a receipt that recorded a pregate is rebound only with a pregate current for HEAD,
  // so a carried receipt never claims the old tree's checks (docs/ship-policy.md#receipt-carry).
  const pregateFile = flag(rest, '--pregate');
  let pregateField: PregateField | undefined;
  if (pregateFile) {
    const local = git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], repoRoot)?.trim();
    if (local !== head) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_PREGATE_STALE', `--pregate verifies this checkout's tree, but the checkout is at ${local?.slice(0, 12) ?? 'no commit'}, not the carried head ${head.slice(0, 12)}; check out ${head.slice(0, 12)} and run gstack-pregate there`);
    const read = pregateFieldFor(repoRoot, pregateFile, head, flag(rest, '--base'));
    if (!read.ok) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_PREGATE_STALE', `--pregate ${pregateFile}: ${read.errors[0]?.code ?? 'invalid'} ${read.errors[0]?.message ?? ''}`.trim());
    pregateField = read.field;
  } else if (receipt.pregate && !rest.includes('--dry-run')) {
    return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_PREGATE_STALE', `the receipt records a pregate for ${receipt.head.slice(0, 12)}; run gstack-pregate at HEAD ${head.slice(0, 12)} and pass --pregate <pregate.json>`);
  }
  let depthField: Partial<ShipReceipt> = {};
  const isAncestor = (commit: string) => !ancestor || spawnSync('git', ['merge-base', '--is-ancestor', commit, head], { cwd: repoRoot, timeout: 30_000 }).status === 0;
  const problems = exceptionProblems(body, receipt, isAncestor);
  if (problems.length) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the receipt's owner exception does not stand: ${problems.join('; ')}; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
  if (receipt.review_depth || receipt.gstack_version) {
    if (!receipt.review_depth) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the receipt records gstack_version but no review_depth, so the queue would refuse it; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
    const checkedOut = git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], repoRoot)?.toLowerCase();
    if (checkedOut !== head) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `--head ${head.slice(0, 12)} is not the checked-out HEAD ${(checkedOut ?? 'none').slice(0, 12)}; the gate scan reads the checkout, so check out ${head.slice(0, 12)} and carry there`);
    const review = receiptReviewAtHead(repoRoot, base, path.dirname(Bun.fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), head);
    const now = review.depth;
    if (review.exclude.state === 'refused') return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `${review.exclude.lines.join('; ')}; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)} once the base policy reads`);
    const digest = review.exclude.state === 'active' ? review.exclude.record.digest : 'none';
    if (!carryExcludeBinds(review.exclude, receipt)) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `review_exclude changed: recorded=${receipt.review_exclude?.digest ?? 'none'} now=${digest} source=${review.exclude.state === 'active' ? review.exclude.record.source : `${base} (no review_exclude_paths)`}; the receipt's digest is the --review-exclude argument write was given, and it names another selection than HEAD ${head.slice(0, 12)} has under the base policy and the two give the PR's files different selections (carry compares those, not the review ledger), so carry does not apply; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
    if (depthBelow(receipt.review_depth.depth, now.depth)) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `HEAD ${head.slice(0, 12)} needs ${now.depth} review depth (${now.reasons.join(', ')}), above the receipt's ${receipt.review_depth.depth}; run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
    depthField = { review_depth: { ...now, depth: deeper(receipt.review_depth.depth, now.depth) }, review_exclude: receiptExclude(review.exclude), review_exclude_fallback: receiptExcludeFallback(review.exclude) };
  }
  // The rebound product_patch_id is HEAD's diff against the carry's base, so a retargeted receipt names that base from now on.
  // A receipt that records a version names HEAD's, read as write reads it: a restamp after a base merge moves it (GST-1030).
  // A head with no version source keeps the recorded one (write --version named it).
  const version = receipt.version === undefined ? undefined : (receiptVersion(repoRoot, head, base) ?? receipt.version);
  const rebound = { ...receipt, ...(version !== undefined ? { version } : {}), ...(retarget ? { base: base.replace(/^origin\//, '') } : {}), ...(pregateField ?? {}), ...depthField };
  const carried = carryReceipt(rebound, head, plan.carry, { tree: headTree, fromTree, productPatchId: headPatch });
  const errors = validateReceipt(carried);
  if (errors.length) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `the carried receipt does not validate: ${errors[0]!.message} at ${errors[0]!.path}`);
  const targetedVerdict = receiptTargetedAtHead(repoRoot, baseRef, carried, head);
  if (!targetedVerdict.ok) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_REFUSED', `${targetedVerdict.line}: ${targetedVerdict.message}, so the queue refuses it too (#3859); run /ship on ${head.slice(0, 12)}`);
  const newBody = placeReceipt(body, carried);
  const line = receiptSummaryLine(carried);
  if (scopedDryRun) return refused('RECEIPT_CARRY_SCOPED_REVIEW', scopedDryRun);
  if (rest.includes('--dry-run')) {
    process.stderr.write(line + '\n');
    process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ skill: 'ship', status: 'dry-run', head, carry: plan.carry }) + '\n' : `CARRY: would carry from ${from.slice(0, 12)} to ${head.slice(0, 12)} (${plan.carry.reason}); nothing written\n`);
    return EXIT.ok;
  }
  const posted = postBody(rest, pr, newBody);
  if (posted) return incomplete(`${posted}; the receipt was not carried`);
  process.stdout.write(`CARRY: carried from ${from.slice(0, 12)} to ${head.slice(0, 12)} (${plan.carry.reason})\n`);
  return writeRunRecord({ receipt: carried, head, pr, source, repoRoot, out: flag(rest, '--out'), json, line, incomplete, extra: { carried_from: carried.carry!.from, carry_reason: carried.carry!.reason } });
}

function sinceDate(repo: string, since: string): string | undefined {
  if (/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}/.test(since)) return since.slice(0, 10);
  const local = git(['log', '-1', '--format=%cI', since]);
  if (local) return local.slice(0, 10);
  const r = gh(['api', `repos/${repo}/commits/${since}`, '--jq', '.commit.committer.date']);
  return r.ok && r.out.trim() ? r.out.trim().slice(0, 10) : undefined;
}

function cmdCensus(rest: string[], json: boolean): number {
  const repo = flag(rest, '--repo');
  const since = flag(rest, '--since');
  if (!repo || !since) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt census: --repo <owner/repo> and --since <tag|date> are required\n${HELP}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  const date = sinceDate(repo, since);
  if (!date) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt census: cannot resolve --since ${since} to a date (not a local tag, and gh could not read it)\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const limit = flag(rest, '--limit') ?? '500';
  const r = gh(['pr', 'list', '--repo', repo, '--state', 'merged', '--search', `merged:>=${date}`, '--limit', limit, '--json', 'number,body,mergedAt,title']);
  if (!r.ok) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt census: gh pr list failed: ${r.err}\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  let prs: CensusPr[];
  try { prs = JSON.parse(r.out); } catch { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt census: gh returned no JSON\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const cohortFile = flag(rest, '--cohort');
  const cohort = cohortFile ? fs.readFileSync(cohortFile, 'utf8').split('\n').map(l => l.trim()).filter(l => l && !l.startsWith('#')) : null;
  const census = computeCensus(repo, date, prs, cohort);
  process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify(census) + '\n' : renderCensus(census));
  return EXIT.ok;
}

/**
 * /ship Step 14.5's doc-cap check: every `docs.caps` entry of the reviewed
 * policy (origin/<base>'s .gstack/ship-policy.json, like every other policy
 * read here; the branch cannot raise its own cap) against the working tree,
 * one DOCS_CAP: line each; any `over` (an absent file counts) exits 1 so the
 * audit blocks before the verification gate. `--policy <file>` reads that
 * file instead, for a repository bootstrapping its policy.
 */
function cmdDocsCaps(rest: string[], json: boolean): number {
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']) ?? process.cwd();
  const policyFile = flag(rest, '--policy');
  let caps: NonNullable<ShipPolicy['docs']>['caps'] = [];
  let source: string;
  if (policyFile !== undefined) {
    if (!fs.existsSync(policyFile)) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt docs-caps: ${policyFile} does not exist\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
    let raw: unknown;
    try { raw = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(policyFile, 'utf8')); } catch (e: any) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt docs-caps: ${policyFile} is not JSON: ${e.message}\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
    const errors = validatePolicy(raw).filter(e => e.path === 'docs' || e.path.startsWith('docs.'));
    if (errors.length) { for (const e of errors) process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt docs-caps', e.code, `${e.message} at ${e.path}`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
    caps = (raw as Partial<ShipPolicy>).docs?.caps ?? [];
    source = policyFile;
  } else {
    const base = flag(rest, '--base') ?? resolveBaseBranch(repoRoot);
    const load = loadPolicyFromBase(repoRoot, base);
    if (isUnavailable(load)) { process.stderr.write(policyUnavailableLine('gstack-ship-receipt docs-caps', base, `${load.detail}; pass --policy <file> to check caps without the base`) + '\n'); return EXIT.refused; }
    const errors = load.errors.filter(e => e.path === 'docs' || e.path.startsWith('docs.'));
    if (errors.length) { for (const e of errors) process.stderr.write(resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt docs-caps', e.code, `${e.message} at ${e.path} (${load.source.label})`) + '\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
    caps = load.policy.docs?.caps ?? [];
    source = load.source.label;
  }
  const results = checkDocsCaps(caps, rel => { try { const st = fs.statSync(path.join(repoRoot, rel)); return st.isFile() ? st.size : null; } catch { return null; } });
  const over = results.filter(r => r.verdict === 'over');
  const lines = results.length ? results.map(docsCapLine) : ['DOCS_CAP: none declared'];
  process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ policy: source, caps: results, over: over.length }) + '\n' : lines.join('\n') + '\n');
  if (!over.length) return EXIT.ok;
  process.stderr.write(resultLineWithDocs('gstack-ship-receipt docs-caps', 'DOCS_AUDIT_BLOCKED', `${over.length} of ${results.length} documentation cap${results.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} over: ${over.map(r => r.path).join(', ')}`) + '\n');
  return EXIT.fail;
}

/** The round grants the branch's approval record holds for this PR (the receipt's review_round_grants). */
function roundGrantsFor(repoRoot: string | undefined, pr: string | undefined): ShipReceipt['review_round_grants'] {
  if (!repoRoot || !pr) return undefined;
  const grants = readReviewRoundGrants(repoRoot).filter(g => String(g.pr) === pr);
  return grants.length ? grants : undefined;
}

/** The PR body from --body or gh, or why it cannot be read. */
function readBody(rest: string[]): { ok: true; body: string; pr?: string } | { ok: false; why: string; fix: string } {
  const bodyFile = flag(rest, '--body');
  if (bodyFile) {
    try { return { ok: true, body: fs.readFileSync(bodyFile, 'utf8') }; } catch (e) { return { ok: false, why: `${bodyFile} is unreadable (${(e as Error).message.split('\n')[0]})`, fix: 'pass a readable --body file' }; }
  }
  const pr = flag(rest, '--pr');
  if (!pr || !/^[1-9]\d*$/.test(pr)) return { ok: false, why: '--pr <n> or --body <file> is required', fix: 'pass the open PR number' };
  const repo = flag(rest, '--repo');
  const r = gh(['pr', 'view', pr, ...(repo ? ['--repo', repo] : []), '--json', 'body']);
  if (!r.ok) return { ok: false, why: `gh pr view ${pr} failed: ${r.err.split('\n')[0]}`, fix: 'check gh auth status and the PR number, then rerun' };
  try { return { ok: true, body: JSON.parse(r.out).body ?? '', pr }; } catch { return { ok: false, why: 'gh returned no JSON body', fix: 'rerun; check gh auth status' }; }
}

/** Write the body back: to --body, to a HOST_PUBLISH hand-off on Capy (GST-3183), else through gh pr edit. */
function postBody(rest: string[], pr: string | undefined, body: string): string | null {
  const bodyFile = flag(rest, '--body');
  if (bodyFile) { fs.writeFileSync(bodyFile, body); return null; }
  const repo = flag(rest, '--repo');
  if (hostPublishes()) {
    const target = repo ?? (process.env.GH_REPO?.trim() || undefined);
    const view = gh(['repo', 'view', ...(target ? [target] : []), '--json', 'nameWithOwner,url']);
    let dest: { repo: string; host: string } | undefined;
    try { const v = JSON.parse(view.out); dest = { repo: String(v.nameWithOwner ?? ''), host: new URL(String(v.url)).host }; } catch { dest = undefined; }
    if (!view.ok || !dest?.repo) return `cannot resolve the repository gh pr edit would have edited (gh repo view${target ? ` ${target}` : ''} --json nameWithOwner,url: ${view.err.split('\n')[0] || 'no repository'}); pass --repo <owner/repo>, nothing was handed off`;
    try { process.stdout.write(handOff({ op: 'pr-body', target: pr, ...dest, parts: [['body', body]] })); }
    catch (e) { return `cannot write the hand-off for the host's PR tool (${(e as Error).message}), nothing was handed off`; }
    return null;
  }
  const tmp = path.join(fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(process.env.TMPDIR ?? '/tmp', 'gstack-runs-')), 'body.md');
  fs.writeFileSync(tmp, body, { mode: 0o600 });
  const edit = gh(['pr', 'edit', pr!, ...(repo ? ['--repo', repo] : []), '--body-file', tmp]);
  fs.rmSync(path.dirname(tmp), { recursive: true, force: true });
  return edit.ok ? null : `gh pr edit failed: ${edit.err}`;
}

/** R51 per pull request: the rounds the PR body records, and what the next head gets (GST-2673). */
function cmdHistory(rest: string[], json: boolean): number {
  const pr = flag(rest, '--pr') ?? '?';
  const read = readBody(rest);
  if (!read.ok) {
    process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt history: ${read.why}; fix: ${read.fix}; until then the review plan counts this run's rounds only\n`);
    process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify({ pr, source: 'unavailable', why: read.why }) + '\n' : `PR_REVIEW_HISTORY: pr=#${pr} source=unavailable\n`);
    return EXIT.fail;
  }
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);
  const head = (flag(rest, '--head') ?? (repoRoot ? git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], repoRoot) : undefined))?.toLowerCase();
  const h = prReviewHistory(read.body);
  const grants = repoRoot && head && /^\d+$/.test(pr) ? readReviewRoundGrants(repoRoot) : [];
  const answer = grants.length ? grantedStop(read.body, grants, { pr: Number(pr), head: head!, run: flag(rest, '--run'), isAncestor: ancestorIn(repoRoot!) }) : null;
  const base = (flag(rest, '--base') ?? (repoRoot ? resolveBaseBranch(repoRoot) : 'main')).replace(/^origin\//, '');
  const baseRef = repoRoot ? [`origin/${base}`, base].find(ref => git(['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', `${ref}^{commit}`], repoRoot)) : undefined;
  const found: ReviewRoundGrant | undefined = answer?.ok ? answer.grant : grants.length ? grantFor(repoRoot!, grants, Number(pr), head!, baseRef) : undefined;
  const claimed = found && !answer?.ok ? receiptRuns(read.body).find(r => r.mark === 'grant' && r.grant === found.approval && r.run !== flag(rest, '--run')) : undefined;
  const grant = claimed ? undefined : found;
  const route = answer?.ok ? { route: 'fix-check' as const, reason: `fix-check grant ${answer.grant.approval} answers the stop at ${answer.stop.head.slice(0, 12)} (run ${answer.stop.run}): one scoped fix-check of the PR's own change since it, for ${answer.grant.findings!.join(', ')}, with no new full review` } : reviewRoute(h, { grant: grant?.approval });
  const flagsLine = `PR_REVIEW_FLAGS: --prior-rounds ${h.rounds} --prior-full ${h.full}${grant ? ` --round-grant ${grant.approval}` : ''}${answer?.ok ? ` --stop ${answer.stop.head}` : ''}`;
  const used = flag(rest, '--run') ? receiptedRun(read.body, flag(rest, '--run')!) : undefined;
  if (json) { process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ pr, ...h, grant: grant ?? null, stop: answer?.ok ? answer.stop : null, route, run_used: used?.head ?? null }) + '\n'); return EXIT.ok; }
  process.stdout.write(`${historyLine(pr, h)}\n${flagsLine}\nPR_REVIEW_ROUTE: ${route.route} (${route.reason})\n${answer && !answer.ok ? `PR_REVIEW_GRANT: not applied (${answer.why})\n` : ''}${claimed ? `PR_REVIEW_GRANT: not applied (grant ${claimed.grant} was claimed by run ${claimed.run}: a grant buys one round)\n` : ''}${used ? `PR_REVIEW_RUN_USED: run=${used.run} receipted at ${used.head.slice(0, 12)}\n` : ''}`);
  return EXIT.ok;
}

const ancestorIn = (repoRoot: string) => (a: string, d: string) => a === d || spawnSync('git', ['merge-base', '--is-ancestor', a, d], { cwd: repoRoot, timeout: 30_000 }).status === 0;

/** Step 9 on NEXT: stop (GST-2968): record the review this run stopped on, so a fix-check grant has one stop to answer. */
function cmdStop(rest: string[]): number {
  const run = flag(rest, '--run'), since = flag(rest, '--since');
  if (!run || !/^[\w.:-]{1,120}$/.test(run) || !since) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt stop: --run <the /ship run id> and --since <REVIEW_SINCE> are required\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);
  if (!repoRoot) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt stop: run it inside the git checkout\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const read = readBody(rest);
  if (!read.ok) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt stop: ${read.why}; fix: ${read.fix}\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const rows = reviewRows(repoRoot);
  if (!rows) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt stop: gstack-review-read failed; nothing recorded\n'); return EXIT.fail; }
  const headNow = git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], repoRoot) ?? '';
  const found = stopFrom(rows, since, { treeOf: c => git(['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', `${c}^{tree}`], repoRoot), onHead: c => ancestorIn(repoRoot)(c, headNow) });
  if (!found.ok) { process.stderr.write(`${resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt stop', 'STOP_UNBOUND', `${found.why}; no stop record, so no fix-check grant can answer this stop`)}\n`); return EXIT.refused; }
  const err = postBody(rest, read.pr, placeRunEntry(read.body, stopMarker({ head: found.head, tree: found.tree, run })));
  if (err) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt stop: ${err}; nothing recorded\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const pr = read.pr ?? flag(rest, '--pr') ?? '<n>';
  const marked = changeRunRecord(repoRoot, 'stop', run, { stop: { head: found.head, tree: found.tree } });
  process.stdout.write(`STOP_RECORD: run=${run} head=${found.head} tree=${found.tree}\n${marked.ok ? '' : `RUN_RECORD: not marked stopped (${marked.why})\n`}NEXT: the lane or its Captain decides: ship with the open notes listed, park, or buy this stop's fix round with gstack-approvals round-grant --pr ${pr} --head ${found.head} --kind fix-check --stop-run ${run} --findings <the open finding ids, comma-separated> --reason "<why>" --by <the lane or its Captain>, then take --round-grant and --stop from the PR_REVIEW_FLAGS: line of gstack-ship-receipt history --pr ${pr} --base <base> --run ${run} in this run, or from a new run's preflight (docs/troubleshooting.md#pr-round-cap)\n`);
  return EXIT.ok;
}

/** Before a granted round's first dispatch: this run spends the grant, so no other run can buy the same round with it. */
async function cmdClaim(rest: string[]): Promise<number> {
  const run = flag(rest, '--run'), id = flag(rest, '--grant');
  if (!run || !/^[\w.:-]{1,120}$/.test(run) || !id) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt claim: --run <the /ship run id> and --grant <approval id> are required\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);
  if (!repoRoot) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt claim: run it inside the git checkout\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const read = readBody(rest);
  if (!read.ok) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt claim: ${read.why}; fix: ${read.fix}\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const grants = readReviewRoundGrants(repoRoot), g = grants.find(x => x.approval === id);
  if (!g) { process.stderr.write(`${resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt claim', 'GRANT_UNKNOWN', `no approved fix-check or round grant ${id} (a gstack-approvals round-grant row, or an owner's review_loop_grant <head> row) in this branch's approval record`)}\n`); return EXIT.refused; }
  const other = receiptRuns(read.body).find(r => r.mark === 'grant' && r.grant === id && r.run !== run);
  if (other) { process.stderr.write(`${resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt claim', 'GRANT_SPENT', `grant ${id} was claimed by run ${other.run}: a grant buys one round; the lane or its Captain records a new one`)}\n`); return EXIT.refused; }
  const held = receiptRuns(read.body).some(r => r.mark === 'grant' && r.grant === id && r.run === run);
  if (!held && g.kind === 'fix-check') {
    const rows = reviewRows(repoRoot);
    if (!rows) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt claim: gstack-review-read failed, so whether a fix-check already spent grant ${id} is unknown; not claimed, so do not dispatch\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
    const { bindFixCheckRow, grantSpent } = await import('../lib/fix-check-clearing');
    if (grantSpent(rows, g, row => bindFixCheckRow(repoRoot, row, grants, { open: true }).ok)) { process.stderr.write(`${resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt claim', 'GRANT_SPENT', `a counted fix-check already read under grant ${id} (it carries the grant, or started after the grant was recorded): a grant buys one round; the lane or its Captain records a new one (docs/troubleshooting.md#pr-round-cap)`)}\n`); return EXIT.refused; }
  }
  const err = postBody(rest, read.pr, placeRunEntry(read.body, grantMarker({ head: g.head, run, grant: id })));
  if (err) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt claim: ${err}; not claimed, so do not dispatch\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const handedOff = !flag(rest, '--body') && hostPublishes();
  const again = handedOff ? { ok: true as const, body: placeRunEntry(read.body, grantMarker({ head: g.head, run, grant: id })) } : readBody(rest);
  if (!again.ok) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt claim: ${again.why}; the claim is unconfirmed, so do not dispatch\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const first = receiptRuns(again.body).find(r => r.mark === 'grant' && r.grant === id);
  if (first?.run !== run) { process.stderr.write(`${resultLine('gstack-ship-receipt claim', 'GRANT_SPENT', `grant ${id} was claimed by run ${first?.run ?? 'another run'} while this run claimed it: a grant buys one round; the lane or its Captain records a new one`)}\n`); return EXIT.refused; }
  const bodyPr = read.pr ?? flag(rest, '--pr');
  const claimPr = g.pr || (bodyPr && /^[1-9]\d*$/.test(bodyPr) ? Number(bodyPr) : undefined);
  const recorded = changeRunRecord(repoRoot, 'claim', run, { claim: { grant: id, ...(g.stop_run ? { stop_run: g.stop_run } : {}), stop_head: g.head, findings: g.findings ?? [], ...(claimPr ? { pr: claimPr } : {}) } });
  if (!recorded.ok && readRunRecord(repoRoot).kind !== 'none') { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt claim: the run record did not take the claim (${recorded.why}); not claimed, so do not dispatch: the PR body already holds run ${run}'s claim, so rerun claim with this same --run once the record is writable (a new run id reads GRANT_SPENT)\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  process.stdout.write(`GRANT_CLAIMED: grant=${id} kind=${g.kind} run=${run} head=${g.head.slice(0, 12)}\n${recorded.ok ? '' : `RUN_RECORD: claim not recorded (${recorded.why})\n`}`);
  return EXIT.ok;
}

/** Step 9: this run's rounds so far, recorded before its receipt exists (a started stub), or voided. */
function cmdStub(rest: string[]): number {
  const run = flag(rest, '--run');
  if (!run || !/^[\w.:-]{1,120}$/.test(run)) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt stub: --run <the /ship run id the receipt write passes too> is required\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const read = readBody(rest);
  if (!read.ok) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt stub: ${read.why}; fix: ${read.fix}\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  let loop: ReturnType<typeof parseReviewLoop>;
  try { loop = flag(rest, '--review-loop') !== undefined ? parseReviewLoop(jsonArg(flag(rest, '--review-loop'))) : { passes: 1, blocking_found: 0, deferred: 0, rounds: 1 }; } catch (e) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt stub: --review-loop: ${(e as Error).message}\n`); return EXIT.usage; }
  if (!loop) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt stub: --review-loop needs {passes, blocking_found, deferred[, fix_checks, rounds, scoped]}\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const head = (flag(rest, '--head') ?? git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD']))?.toLowerCase();
  if (!head || !/^[0-9a-f]{40,64}$/.test(head)) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt stub: cannot resolve HEAD\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const status = rest.includes('--void') ? 'voided' : 'started';
  const err = postBody(rest, read.pr, placeRunEntry(read.body, runStub({ head, run, status, loop })));
  if (err) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt stub: ${err}; the run is not recorded\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const repoRoot = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);
  if (repoRoot) changeRunRecord(repoRoot, 'beat', run);
  process.stdout.write(`RUN_STUB: run=${run} status=${status} rounds=${loop.passes} head=${head.slice(0, 12)}\n`);
  return EXIT.ok;
}

/** gstack-ship-run abandon's PR-body half (GST-3260): a mark:abandoned entry in the runs block naming the run, who ended it and why. */
function cmdAbandoned(rest: string[]): number {
  const run = flag(rest, '--run'), by = flag(rest, '--by')?.trim(), reason = flag(rest, '--reason')?.trim();
  if (!run || !/^[\w.:-]{1,128}$/.test(run) || !by || !reason || /[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/.test(by + reason)) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt abandoned: --run <id>, --by <who> and --reason <one line> are required\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const read = readBody(rest);
  if (!read.ok) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt abandoned: ${read.why}; fix: ${read.fix}\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  const head = git(['rev-parse', 'HEAD'])?.toLowerCase();
  if (!head) { process.stderr.write('gstack-ship-receipt abandoned: cannot resolve HEAD\n'); return EXIT.usage; }
  const err = postBody(rest, read.pr, placeRunEntry(read.body, abandonMarker({ head, run, by, reason })));
  if (err) { process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt abandoned: ${err}; not marked\n`); return EXIT.fail; }
  process.stdout.write(`RUN_ABANDON_MARK: run=${run} head=${head.slice(0, 12)}\n`);
  return EXIT.ok;
}

async function main(argv: string[]): Promise<number> {
  const [cmd, ...rest] = argv;
  const json = rest.includes('--json');
  if (!cmd || cmd === '--help' || cmd === '-h' || cmd === 'help') { process.stdout.write(HELP + '\n'); return cmd ? EXIT.ok : EXIT.usage; }
  if (cmd === 'write') return cmdWrite(rest, json);
  if (cmd === 'read') return cmdRead(rest, json);
  if (cmd === 'result') return cmdResult(rest, json);
  if (cmd === 'census') return cmdCensus(rest, json);
  if (cmd === 'carry') return cmdCarry(rest, json);
  if (cmd === 'docs-caps') return cmdDocsCaps(rest, json);
  if (cmd === 'history') return cmdHistory(rest, json);
  if (cmd === 'stub') return cmdStub(rest);
  if (cmd === 'stop') return cmdStop(rest);
  if (cmd === 'claim') return cmdClaim(rest);
  if (cmd === 'abandoned') return cmdAbandoned(rest);
  process.stderr.write(`gstack-ship-receipt: unknown command ${cmd}\n${HELP}\n`);
  return EXIT.usage;
}

process.exitCode = await main(process.argv.slice(2));
